Default shared list data (ARCEP-derived)
----------------------------------------

Default French demarchage / call-center prefix entries shipped or generated by
`pnpm lists:seed` are **derived** from ARCEP open data and are **not** a dump of
third-party community blocklists (ADR-002).

Source dataset:

- Title: Ressources en numérotation téléphonique (MAJNUM)
- Publisher: ARCEP (via data.gouv.fr)
- Dataset page: https://www.data.gouv.fr/datasets/ressources-en-numerotation-telephonique
- Typical CSV: https://extranet.arcep.fr/uploads/MAJNUM.csv
- Upstream license: **Licence Ouverte 2.0** (Etalab)

Our published list policy for these derived entries is **CC BY-SA** (ADR-001 /
ADR-002). Each `list_entries` row stores `attribution` and `source_date` so
operators and clients can show provenance.

Licence Ouverte 2.0 requires attribution of the source and the date of the last
update when redistributing or creating derived works. Re-run `pnpm lists:seed`
after deploy (or use `ARCEP_SEED_FIXTURE=1` offline) so attribution dates stay
accurate.

Do not vendor Saracroche, Begone, or PhoneBlock datasets as repository defaults.
